    "summary": "T6 now uses precise device/inode proof to classify rejected rename acknowledgements: unchanged prior => not_replaced, owned temporary now visible => replaced, unprovable => uncertain. Coordinator-owned prior/candidate fences survive discarded execution objects and subsequent connections, rejecting structurally valid third states and bad hashes/sources until exact restoration. Accepted-on-disk recovery re-acks the identical mapping. Distinct pending branch follows the approved LLD verbatim: 'Recovery after a pre-replacement failure can retry attribution only if no accepted mapping is actually on disk.' The new both-route test proves explicit re-attribution is allowed ONLY for that pending branch; it is not loss of an accepted mapping. All 166 scoped tests and typecheck pass.",
